<title>TURKEY: Turkey increases tax on petroleum products.</title>
<headline>Turkey increases tax on petroleum products.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey has increased consumption taxes on petroleum products by between 20 and 90 percentage points, according to an announcement in the official gazette on Monday.</p>
<p>Tax on lead-free petrol increased from 180 perecent to 270 percent, normal petrol from 190 to 280 percent, diesel fuel from 130 to 180 percent and domestic fuel oil from 45 to 70 percent.</p>
<p>Along with the changes in consumer petroleum prices, prices from the refineries increased by between 15 and 32 percent.</p>
</text>
